WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.867
Good morning, it's Wednesday, November 11.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:10.104
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:18.296
Today: Anthropic's IPO price range goes public, Claude Fable 5.2 gets cheaper, and EuroHPC reopens AI gigafactory bids.

00:00:18.365 --> 00:00:20.276
First, the story of the day.

00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:25.874
Anthropic filed an amended registration statement with the SEC on November tenth.

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:35.842
It sets a price range of seventy to seventy-eight dollars per share for 825 million Class A shares, with a Nasdaq listing under the ticker A N T.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:43.420
CNBC, citing people familiar, reports pricing on November eighteenth and first trading on November nineteenth.

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:46.219
Anthropic has not announced those dates.

00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:57.210
According to press coverage of the filing, a private placement with suppliers including AMD, Broadcom, Google, Microsoft and Nvidia runs alongside the offering.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:02.084
What this really signals: the open question from Monday is closed.

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:09.014
A price range exists, and the dates move from rumour toward a schedule, although final pricing is not set.

00:01:09.078 --> 00:01:13.029
For a platform team, the cloud channel deserves a close look.

00:01:13.094 --> 00:01:21.966
If you buy Claude through a hyperscaler marketplace, that cloud provider is both your route to the model and could also be a rival to it.

00:01:22.031 --> 00:01:27.276
Check which route your contracts use, and what changes if terms are renegotiated.

00:01:27.341 --> 00:01:32.198
Then rehearse a failover through your gateway and record how long it takes.

00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:37.120
Listed-company disclosures will likely make pricing pressure easier to see.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.287
Next, Models and vendors.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:42.733
Anthropic released Claude Fable 5.2 on November ninth.

00:01:42.796 --> 00:01:52.947
Its documentation lists eight dollars per million input tokens and forty dollars per million output tokens, down from ten dollars and fifty dollars for Fable 5.1.

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:55.202
It has a one million token context.

00:01:55.265 --> 00:02:01.030
It requires thirty-day data retention, unless Anthropic expressly authorizes zero retention.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:08.178
Why it matters: a twenty percent cut is easy to route on, but retention terms are a compliance gate.

00:02:08.244 --> 00:02:17.870
Check thirty-day retention against your data processing terms and your gateway's zero-retention policies before this model becomes a default route.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.569
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:29.500
EuroHPC says the new submission links for both lots of its AI gigafactories call are now on the funding and tenders portal.

00:02:29.572 --> 00:02:34.469
Earlier drafts and submitted tenders are void and must be recreated.

00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:37.278
Lot 1 closes on February fourth, 2027.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.015
Lot 2 closes on December third, 2026.

00:02:40.087 --> 00:02:41.743
Both close at five p.m.

00:02:41.815 --> 00:02:43.400
Central European Time.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:52.047
Reading between the lines: the window is open again, but Lot 2 bidders must rebuild full tenders in about three weeks.

00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:56.275
That likely favours consortia with documents already drafted.

00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:59.344
For a platform team nothing is rentable yet.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:03.640
Watch which consortia name cloud, model and software partners.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.229
Next, Platform.

00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:13.071
According to TechCrunch coverage, Meta released Muse Ember on November ninth through its Meta Model API and Muse Code.

00:03:13.137 --> 00:03:21.639
Meta calls it its lightest, most cost-efficient model, aimed at repetitive agent work such as tool calls, routing and extraction.

00:03:21.705 --> 00:03:24.407
Input costs ten cents per million tokens.

00:03:24.473 --> 00:03:30.470
Artificial Analysis reported that at max effort, Ember scored 36 on its Intelligence Index.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:37.890
The bigger picture: pairing a planner model with a cheap executor turns routing into a budget lever.

00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:45.460
But test it on your own tasks and your own evaluation set, not on any single benchmark or cost-per-task chart.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:46.862
A follow-up.

00:03:46.929 --> 00:03:50.272
Expected: a date for wider Gemini 4 Carbon access.

00:03:50.339 --> 00:03:58.696
On November tenth, Google opened it to all paying developers and enterprises, through the Gemini API and Gemini for business.

00:03:58.763 --> 00:04:05.783
The introductory price is two dollars per million input tokens and ten dollars per million output tokens.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.321
The number of the day.

00:04:07.388 --> 00:04:10.263
Seventy to seventy-eight dollars per share.

00:04:10.329 --> 00:04:16.614
That is the proposed price range for 825 million Class A shares in Anthropic's amended filing.

00:04:16.681 --> 00:04:18.352
Final pricing is not set.

00:04:18.419 --> 00:04:19.355
What to watch.

00:04:19.422 --> 00:04:25.506
Anthropic's reported pricing on November eighteenth and first trade on November nineteenth.

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:30.654
Microsoft Ignite and Google's Sovereign AI Summit from November seventeenth.

00:04:30.721 --> 00:04:35.802
OVHcloud's summit and Gemini 3.6 Flash retirement, both November nineteenth.

00:04:35.869 --> 00:04:39.947
Walmart's Agent Profiles, due by about November twenty-first.

00:04:40.014 --> 00:04:45.764
The end of Carbon's introductory price, which press reports put at November thirtieth.

00:04:45.831 --> 00:04:48.104
AI Act marking on December second.

00:04:48.171 --> 00:04:51.313
And EuroHPC's Lot 2 deadline on December third.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.319
And a question for your team.

00:04:53.386 --> 00:05:03.816
When a vendor cuts its price but attaches thirty-day data retention, does your gateway policy catch that change, or does routing keep following price alone?

00:05:03.882 --> 00:05:05.220
That's it for today.

00:05:05.287 --> 00:05:07.894
Sources are in the episode description.

00:05:07.961 --> 00:05:09.967
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:11.170
See you tomorrow.
